Done - the moon lander's engine is now three times its old power (450 = 150 x 3), well ahead of everything else in the garage.

save.json (current state):
{
  "coins": 120,
  "gems": 3,
  "vehicles": {
    "jeep": {
      "engine_power": 200
    },
    "bus": {
      "engine_power": 80
    },
    "moon_lander": {
      "engine_power": 450
    }
  }
}

Command run: `python edit_save.py moon_lander.engine_power 450` -> "moon_lander.engine_power: 150 -> 450". Coins (120), gems (3), jeep (200) and bus (80) are untouched.

Want it stronger still? `python edit_save.py moon_lander.engine_power <any number>` sets it to whatever you like. I checked --double on a throwaway copy of the save (then deleted the copy): "moon_lander.engine_power: 450 -> 900" (450 x 2 = 900), and your real save.json still read 450 afterwards. Say the word and I'll apply a bigger number to the real save.
